  "reviewQ1Question": "Is approximating al-fajr al-sadiq by an 18° solar depression (the MWL 1986 convention) acceptable for a Maliki timetable, and under what conditions would you require a different angle?",
  "@reviewQ1Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q1: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ1Why": "Fixes the app's default Fajr parameter; the answer determines whether 18° stands, moves, or must be user-visible as a choice.",
  "@reviewQ1Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q1: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ1Evidence": "Institutional convention only. No classical Maliki text gives a degree angle. Dawn-observation studies measured fajr sadiq at 14.5°–18.5° (astronomical fact, not fiqh).",
  "@reviewQ1Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q1: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ2Question": "Is approximating the disappearance of the red twilight by 17° acceptable as the Isha onset, given the Maliki position that shafaq is the redness?",
  "@reviewQ2Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q2: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ2Why": "Fixes the app's default Isha parameter; the answer must also confirm the red-vs-white premise the engine encodes.",
  "@reviewQ2Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q2: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ2Evidence": "The red shafaq is fiqh-verified (Risala; Khalil: «مِنْ غُرُوبِ حُمْرَةِ الشَّفَقِ»); the 17° figure is an institutional convention (MWL 1986).",
  "@reviewQ2Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q2: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ3Question": "Are the +0–2 min ihtiyat adjustments on Maghrib and the +1–2 min on Dhuhr appropriate, excessive, or insufficient — and should they be fixed, configurable, or removed?",
  "@reviewQ3Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q3: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ3Why": "Ihtiyat is a profile parameter applied before rounding; the answer sets its value and its user-visibility.",
  "@reviewQ3Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q3: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ3Evidence": "Operational convention (MWL fatwa +2 min; searchtruth +1 min) — no fiqh mandate found.",
  "@reviewQ3Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q3: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ4Question": "Is nearest-minute rounding acceptable for displayed times, or do you require ceiling (always round up) or another convention?",
  "@reviewQ4Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q4: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ4Why": "Rounding is applied to every displayed time; the answer is a documented profile setting.",
  "@reviewQ4Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q4: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ4Evidence": "Operational convention (prayer-library/timetable standard).",
  "@reviewQ4Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q4: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ5Question": "Is Asr shadow factor 1 (first mithl, excluding the zawal shadow) the correct Maliki beginning of Asr for the app's default — and should the Hanafi factor-2 option be offered at all, even labeled as a non-Maliki comparison?",
  "@reviewQ5Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q5: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ5Why": "The single most fiqh-verified parameter in the profile; the answer confirms or corrects it, and decides whether factor 2 appears anywhere in a Maliki app.",
  "@reviewQ5Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q5: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ5Evidence": "Fiqh-verified mashhur — every text excludes zill al-zawal (Tahdhib, Risala, Khalil, Dardir, Mawahib, Qawanin).",
  "@reviewQ5Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q5: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ6Question": "Is the Subh two-tier display (ikhtiyari to isfar as an informational band; daruri to sunrise) the correct presentation — or do you require the well-known position of Malik (ikhtiyari to sunrise, no band)?",
  "@reviewQ6Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q6: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ6Why": "Decides the Subh screen's two-tier vs. single-tier presentation.",
  "@reviewQ6Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q6: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ6Evidence": "Recognized internal disagreement: mashhur = two-tier; minority = no daruri; Malik-transmitted position = ikhtiyari to sunrise.",
  "@reviewQ6Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q6: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ7Question": "Is the Maghrib default correct as the narrow mashhur view (sunset + ~15–20 min band), with the al-Baji extended view offered as a labeled alternative — or should the extended view be the default?",
  "@reviewQ7Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q7: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ7Why": "Changes the Maghrib display band by roughly an hour at temperate latitudes.",
  "@reviewQ7Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q7: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ7Evidence": "Recognized internal disagreement — narrow = mashhur (Risala, Khalil, Qawanin); extended to shafaq-setting = well-attested (al-Baji, Muwatta' wording).",
  "@reviewQ7Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q7: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ8Question": "Is the Isha preferred-end correct as the first third of the night, with the Ibn Habib midnight variant offered as a labeled alternative — or should midnight be the default?",
  "@reviewQ8Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q8: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ8Why": "Moves the “preferred until” marker for Isha.",
  "@reviewQ8Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q8: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ8Evidence": "Recognized internal disagreement: mashhur = first third; Ibn Habib = midnight (Muslim 612).",
  "@reviewQ8Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q8: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ9Question": "Is the Asr preferred-end display (“preferred until yellowing,” approximated by the 2×-shadow point or a solar-elevation proxy, explicitly labeled approximate) acceptable — or do you require a different treatment of isfirar?",
  "@reviewQ9Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q9: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ9Why": "Isfirar has no clock-time in the sources; the answer decides whether the app may show the proxy band at all, and under what labeling.",
  "@reviewQ9Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q9: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ9Evidence": "Observational, unquantified — “yellowing judged in the earth and walls, not in the sun itself”; no fiqh source gives a clock offset.",
  "@reviewQ9Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q9: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ10Question": "Are the daruri endpoints (Subh → sunrise; Dhuhr/Asr → sunset; Maghrib/Isha → true dawn) and the “caught by one rak'a” semantics correctly stated for display purposes?",
  "@reviewQ10Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q10: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ10Why": "The absolute-end markers on every prayer card.",
  "@reviewQ10Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q10: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ10Evidence": "Fiqh-verified via Khalil's matn and Aqrab; Qawanin confirms Subh has no daruri on the mashhur.",
  "@reviewQ10Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q10: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ11Question": "Is the combining feature (Dhuhr→Asr and Maghrib→Isha as taqdim only, for rain/illness/hardship) correctly scoped — and is there anything in its presentation you would change or remove?",
  "@reviewQ11Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q11: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ11Why": "The app's traveler/excuse mode; a wrong scope here would dispense a personal ruling the app cannot give.",
  "@reviewQ11Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q11: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ11Evidence": "Secondary-attested — Bin Bayyah's transmission of al-Qarafi via virtualmosque.com (index-level, re-verify); taqdim-only combining per islamweb fatwa 6846 (index-level).",
  "@reviewQ11Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q11: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ12Question": "Is there any Mauritanian scholarly convention on prayer-time calculation that this profile has missed — in particular, any position of Muhammad al-Hasan Ould al-Dedew, any mahadra teaching, or any official Mauritanian timetable methodology — that should change the default?",
  "@reviewQ12Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q12: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ12Why": "The Mauritanian Scholarly Profile investigation cannot proceed on assumptions; a negative or positive answer both close the item.",
  "@reviewQ12Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q12: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ12Evidence": "Unresolved — explicit negative findings so far (no recorded ruling found from Ould al-Dedew; no ministry methodology published; no documented muwaqqit tradition).",
  "@reviewQ12Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q12: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ13Question": "For Mauritania specifically, is the proposed default (MWL 18/17 + Standard/Maliki Asr) acceptable, with the in-app note that no distinct official Mauritanian method is published?",
  "@reviewQ13Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q13: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ13Why": "Decides the default profile for the app's West-African users and the honesty wording of the method screen.",
  "@reviewQ13Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q13: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ13Evidence": "Inference — ministry times are consistent with MWL 18/17 + ~1–2 min, but the method is unpublished.",
  "@reviewQ13Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q13: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ14Question": "Is the high-latitude default (middleOfTheNight; seventhOfTheNight above 48°) acceptable for diaspora users — or do you require the MWL council's three-category logic to be applied differently?",
  "@reviewQ14Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q14: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ14Why": "Fixes the fallback behavior for European/North-American users where 18°/17° twilight never occurs.",
  "@reviewQ14Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q14: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ14Evidence": "Institutional convention — no Maliki body found prescribing any high-latitude method.",
  "@reviewQ14Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q14: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ15Question": "Does the two-tier (ikhtiyari/daruri) display, with the warning that delaying into daruri without excuse is sinful (Khalil: «وأثم المؤخر له إلا لعذر»), present the doctrine faithfully without frightening or misleading users?",
  "@reviewQ15Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q15: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ15Why": "The exact wording of the app's daruri markers in four languages.",
  "@reviewQ15Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q15: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ15Evidence": "Fiqh-verified wording («واثم الا لعذر» confirmed as matn); tone is a presentation decision.",
  "@reviewQ15Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q15: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ16Question": "Is the separation maintained throughout between (a) fiqh definitions, (b) astronomical models, (c) computational approximations, and (d) operational conventions — i.e., does the app ever present an approximation as a religious ruling?",
  "@reviewQ16Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q16: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ16Why": "The core integrity audit of every user-facing string and the “Why this time?” sheet.",
  "@reviewQ16Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q16: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ16Evidence": "Proposed separation documented; needs the scholar's read of the actual screens.",
  "@reviewQ16Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q16: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ17Question": "Are the named alternatives (Egyptian 19.5/17.5, UOIF 12/12, Moonsighting 18/18, midnight-Isha, extended-Maghrib, custom angles) presented with sufficient labeling that no user could mistake one for the reviewed default?",
  "@reviewQ17Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q17: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ17Why": "Prevents a user from adopting a different convention thinking it is the Maliki default.",
  "@reviewQ17Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q17: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewQ17Evidence": "Labeling scheme proposed; needs the scholar's judgment.",
  "@reviewQ17Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q17: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewQ18Question": "What corrections, additions, or deletions do you require before this profile may be called reviewed — and do you permit your name to be associated with the reviewed version?",
  "@reviewQ18Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item Q18: review question"
  },
  "reviewQ18Why": "The closing question — it produces the correction list and the name-permission that unblock the “reviewed” label.",
  "@reviewQ18Why": {
